[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":110},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news-detail-university-of-texas-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa-216":3},{"news":4,"more":27},{"id":5,"slug":6,"title":7,"content":8,"authorName":9,"authorId":10,"status":11,"recommended":12,"datePosted":13,"deadline":14,"images":15,"notifiedAt":14,"notifiedBy":14,"createdAt":13,"updatedAt":21,"categories":22,"readTime":24},216,"university-of-texas-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa-216","University Of Texas Scholarship 2026: Fully Funded In Usa","\u003Cp>The University of Texas Scholarship offers a graduate assistantship that covers the tuition fees of selected candidates and a living stipend of $21,000 per year.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The scholarship is applicable to master’s studies for international and home students.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>University of Texas Scholarship Abstract\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: University of Texas\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study Abroad\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fcategory\u002Fscholarship\u002Fscholarships-in-usa\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study-In-USA\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Location: Tyler\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Category: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Postgraduate Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fmasters-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Masters Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Tuition\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>$21,000 Stipend per year\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Deadline: June 10, 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>University of Texas Scholarship Details\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Dr. Matthew Greenwold (\u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greenwoldlab.com\u002F\">https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greenwoldlab.com\u002F\u003C\u002Fa>) and Jessica Coleman at the University of Texas at Tyler in collaboration with Dr. Rebecca Bracken at the Gulf Coast Bird Observatory (\u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.gcbo.org\u002F\">https:\u002F\u002Fwww.gcbo.org\u002F\u003C\u002Fa>) are seeking two highly motivated graduate students (MS level) to start this Fall 2026 semester or Spring 2027 semester. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Specifically, we’re recruiting students to work on a comprehensive study of \u003Cstrong>Chuck-will’s-widow\u003C\u002Fstrong> in Texas.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>This will involve monitoring breeding patterns in Texas, migration patterns using satellite transmitters, and occupancy modeling. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>University of Texas Scholarship 2026 Benefits\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>University of Texas Scholarship 2026 Requirements\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To be eligible for the University of Texas Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Have a bachelor’s degree with at least a GPA of 3.25.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A \u003Cstrong>strong preference\u003C\u002Fstrong> will be given to candidates with bird banding experience or experience handling wild bird species. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>University of Texas Scholarship Required Documents\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>While applying for the 2026 University of Texas Scholarship, you will be required to submit the following documents;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>a brief cover letter,\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>CV, and if available,\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>unofficial transcripts\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>How To Apply for University of Texas Scholarship 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To apply for the University of Texas Scholarship 2026, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Interested applicants are encouraged to email\u003C\u002Fstrong> Dr. Matthew Greenwold (\u003Ca href=\"mailto:mgreenwold@uttyler.edu\">mgreenwold@uttyler.edu\u003C\u002Fa>) and Jessica Coleman (\u003Ca href=\"mailto:jcoleman@uttyler.edu\">jcoleman@uttyler.edu\u003C\u002Fa>) with the required documents by \u003Cstrong>June 10th\u003C\u002Fstrong>. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>APPLY HERE: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fjobs.rwfm.tamu.edu\u002Fview-job\u002F?id=116196\">https:\u002F\u002Fjobs.rwfm.tamu.edu\u002Fview-job\u002F?id=116196\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>","linkskool",16,"published",0,"2026-05-07 17:09:52",null,[16],{"fileName":17,"oldFileName":17,"type":18,"file":19,"url":20},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Funiversity-of-texas-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa\u002F69fcb95030da35.25010265_screenshot 2026-05-07 164659.png","image","","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Funiversity-of-texas-scholarship-2